---
title: Installing Diorama64
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

You need a Paper Mario (US) ROM. To dump one from a cartridge, see the [dumping guide](https://dumping.guide/carts/nintendo/n64#methods). Diorama64 accepts `.z64`, `.n64`, and `.v64` files.

If you'd rather use your own editor and a terminal, see [Working without Diorama64](/papermario-dx/developing/without-diorama64).

## Download and install

{% tabs %}
{% tabitem label="Windows" %}
  {% steps %}
  1. [Download Diorama64 for Windows](https://diorama64.starhaven.dev/download/windows).
  2. Run the installer.
  {% /steps %}
{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="macOS" %}
  {% steps %}
  1. [Download Diorama64 for macOS](https://diorama64.starhaven.dev/download/macos). It runs on both Intel and Apple silicon Macs.
  2. Open the downloaded `.dmg` file, and drag **Diorama64** to the **Applications** folder.
  3. Open Diorama64 from your **Applications** folder.
  {% /steps %}
{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="Linux" %}
  {% steps %}
  1. [Download Diorama64 for Linux](https://diorama64.starhaven.dev/download/linux). It's an AppImage for x86_64.
  2. Make the file executable, such as by running `chmod +x Diorama64-*.AppImage`.
  3. Run the AppImage.
  {% /steps %}
{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="Nix" %}
  Run Diorama64 straight from its repository:

  ```sh
  nix run git+https://tangled.org/starhaven.dev/diorama64
  ```
{% /tabitem %}
{% /tabs %}

## Creating a mod

{% steps %}
1. Select **Mod > New Mod...**.
2. Enter a **Mod name**. Diorama64 names the mod's folder after it. To keep the mod somewhere else, select **Browse…** and choose a folder.
3. Select **Create**.
4. The first time you create a mod, Diorama64 asks for your ROM. Select **Choose ROM…**, then choose your ROM and select **Use ROM**. Diorama64 keeps the ROM on your computer for every mod you make later.
{% /steps %}
